509	650,1205,1512,2215 - 725,1790,885,2045 - 805,1960,1082,2215 - 1300,1865,1512,2215 - 1140,1990,1512,2215 - 1250,1880,1300,1990	509. Yellow Dogtooth-Violet.	The whole plant: two long mottled and blotched leaves sheathing a slender scape, which bears one nodding lily-like flower with recurved divisions.
510	805,1960,1082,2215 - 805,1960,822,2010	510. The bulb.	A small pointed coated bulb with fibrous roots spreading from its base and the scape rising from its tip.
511	1140,1865,1682,2228 - 1140,1865,1255,1990	511. Perianth laid open, and stamens.	The six narrow pointed divisions of the perianth spread out in a fan, each with a stamen and its long erect anther.
512	1540,1375,1605,1820 - 1588,1770,1605,1810	512. The pistil, enlarged.	A single pistil: an oblong ovary on a short stalk, tapering into a long club-shaped style with the united stigmas at its tip.
513	725,1790,885,2012	513. Lower half of a pod, cut across and magnified.	A rounded pod on its stalk, cut across to show three cells, each holding its seeds.
